{"id": "EUVD-2026-96903", "enisaUuid": "04ec0a5c-af4e-3384-990c-187ae0da70cd", "description": "Traccar through 6.16.0 contains a weak password recovery vulnerability that allows attackers to reuse password reset tokens as session credentials because TokenManager does not bind tokens to a purpose. Attackers holding a leaked reset link can obtain a full session via /api/session or change passwords via /api/password/update, retaining access for seven days even after the victim resets their password.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:47:31", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/traccar-token-purpose-confusion", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar/blob/cfab560c79ee9c9eaa41c79c6df351e820d6284b/src/main/java/org/traccar/api/signature/TokenManager.java#L47-L109", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar/blob/cfab560c79ee9c9eaa41c79c6df351e820d6284b/src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/PasswordResource.java#L72-L90", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar/blob/cfab560c79ee9c9eaa41c79c6df351e820d6284b/src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/SessionResource.java#L77-L93", "https://github.com/traccar/traccar", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/traccar-through-6.16.0-weak-password-recovery-via-tokenmanager-token-purpose-confusion"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108737", "GHSA-2qrx-94v4-66vp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7a792ed5-f809-305e-b019-63fd05dc887a", "product": {"name": "traccar", "vendor": {"name": "traccar"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.16.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "317e15c1-05fe-3be4-9ca8-6a9c05f13bf4", "vendor": {"name": "traccar"}}], "isExploited": false}